WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.083
- Top reasons why I love being black.

00:00:04.412 --> 00:00:06.534
Oh my god, you see this skin?

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:09.266
- There is so much richness and history

00:00:09.266 --> 00:00:10.773
behind my skin.

00:00:10.773 --> 00:00:12.671
- I just love the soul, like I don't know

00:00:12.671 --> 00:00:13.989
how to describe it other than that.

00:00:13.989 --> 00:00:15.424
- Do you see this skin?

00:00:15.424 --> 00:00:17.877
- We're not just one part of the box.

00:00:17.877 --> 00:00:19.312
We encompass everything.

00:00:19.312 --> 00:00:20.729
- This is what I think about black culture

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:23.063
I think about how powerful
it is, I think about the fact

00:00:23.063 --> 00:00:24.973
that our ancestors are the ones that you

00:00:24.973 --> 00:00:25.885
could not break.

00:00:25.885 --> 00:00:28.741
- If I woke up, and I was
anything other than black,

00:00:28.741 --> 00:00:30.718
I would be completely jealous.

00:00:30.718 --> 00:00:32.846
- Black twitter is lit, you know.

00:00:32.846 --> 00:00:35.662
- My melanin pop, that's
why this outfit works,

00:00:35.662 --> 00:00:37.717
you don't see nobody
else rocking a baby blue

00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:39.427
outfit out here like this.

00:00:39.427 --> 00:00:41.301
- Black loves. Whenever we come together

00:00:41.301 --> 00:00:42.964
and we, know what I'm saying, this is like

00:00:42.964 --> 00:00:43.913
nothing else.

00:00:43.913 --> 00:00:46.608
- Before I came to America,
being black was the

00:00:46.608 --> 00:00:50.201
only thing I knew. For
me, it's my identity.

00:00:50.201 --> 00:00:52.163
Nobody can take this away from me.

00:00:52.163 --> 00:00:54.366
- Black just doesn't have one definition.

00:00:54.366 --> 00:00:56.128
My black is different from her black.

00:00:56.128 --> 00:00:58.235
- I can come to a place
like this and just see

00:00:58.235 --> 00:01:00.647
so much beauty and diversity, see so many

00:01:00.647 --> 00:01:03.019
people who are just like
proud of their melanin.

00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:04.530
And like, dancing to our own music.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.875
- The originality and the strength.

00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:07.721
Never duplicated, always imitated.

00:01:07.721 --> 00:01:09.975
But just the strength and
the creativity that we have

00:01:09.975 --> 00:01:11.059
in our culture.

00:01:11.059 --> 00:01:13.086
- We're loud and we're proud of it.

00:01:13.086 --> 00:01:15.682
And the culture is so fricking rich.

00:01:15.682 --> 00:01:17.138
- And it's like, wherever
you go in the world,

00:01:17.138 --> 00:01:19.397
is a kind of unity. Like,
everyone knows the nod.

00:01:19.397 --> 00:01:21.058
- I just love all of our
features. Like there's

00:01:21.058 --> 00:01:23.412
nothing like it. The
sun can't even break us.

00:01:23.412 --> 00:01:25.682
- We just created this
whole culture that's like,

00:01:25.682 --> 00:01:27.587
it's influencing the entire world now.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.083
- As it says on my poster here,

00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:33.520
I am dipped in chocolate,
bronzed in elegance,

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:37.927
enabled with grace, and
I am toasted with beauty.

00:01:37.927 --> 00:01:40.689
That is why I love being black.

00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:42.647
- [Voiceover] I think that
it's amazing to come from

00:01:42.647 --> 00:01:47.271
a people who have overcome,
and who strive to be great,

00:01:47.271 --> 00:01:48.336
people who are great.

00:01:48.336 --> 00:01:50.599
- Black excellence, shout out
to all the recent graduates.

00:01:50.599 --> 00:01:53.785
- We always are given
scraps, like chitlins,

00:01:53.785 --> 00:01:56.346
the bottoms of the bottom,
and we take those things,

00:01:56.346 --> 00:01:58.275
and we make them into cultural staples.

00:01:58.275 --> 00:01:59.999
- Collectively, we're
one, but individually,

00:01:59.999 --> 00:02:01.311
we're beautiful.

00:02:01.311 --> 00:02:04.327
- Some black people, you can't
pinpoint back where exactly

00:02:04.327 --> 00:02:06.361
you came from, but you can feel it.

00:02:06.361 --> 00:02:08.416
- We're not confined to
one thing. I learned from

00:02:08.416 --> 00:02:09.890
different people, different cultures,

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.532
and we're all brought together
by the color of our skin.

00:02:11.532 --> 00:02:13.275
- Black women can wear any color

00:02:13.275 --> 00:02:15.405
of the rainbow and look amazing.

00:02:15.405 --> 00:02:19.155
- Amongst like the discrimination,
and the racial tension

00:02:19.155 --> 00:02:22.923
in our country, I'd still
wouldn't rather be anything else.

00:02:22.923 --> 00:02:25.918
- We are like a community
of beauty and resiliency.

00:02:25.918 --> 00:02:28.083
- In all honesty, we're just poppin'.

00:02:28.083 --> 00:02:31.171
- Black Christians, black lives matter!

00:02:31.171 --> 00:02:34.665
- I love it! Like honestly,
there's so many things.

00:02:34.665 --> 00:02:37.081
- Come on now, look at our
fashion. Look at our rules.

00:02:37.081 --> 00:02:39.622
Look at where we come from.

00:02:39.622 --> 00:02:42.455
Why wouldn't you want to be black?

